The trick that does work, as indicated by others, is
to right click on a clear part of the window's title
bar, select "Edit => Mark", and walk the cursor from
top left to bottom right (or across the portion you
want to capture) with the <SHIFT> key held down,
using the arrow keys. Right click on a clear part of
the window's title bar, select "Edit => Copy"
(alternately, just type <ENTER>), which captures the
selected text. Next, open a text document of any
kind, and paste the text using <CTRL-v> or
<ALT-E><ALT-P>. If planning to reproduce the image
for any purpose, make sure you have a fixed pitch
font selected, or it will look lousy.

